{"agent":"dedupe-t1-evalset","data":{"body":"Per D-no-duplicates and R-dedupe-matchers. FTS5 picks top-50 candidates per kind from index.db; stdlib TF-IDF cosine reranks (IDF stored in index.db); without FTS5 compare against everything. [dedupe] config: on_match (ask|warn|off), show_floor 0.35, ask_threshold 0.55, max_candidates 3, min_words 8, kinds. Cross-kind candidates (a bug sees open tasks and vice versa). Flags: text names an existing id; same item. Acceptance on the evaluation set: duplicates R@3 >= 0.95; related R@5 >= 0.9; lenient precision at the ask threshold >= 0.75; hard negatives above it <= 20%; p95 < 50 ms at 6k records; same results without FTS5; no new dependency. store.py is also in B194/B-semantic-recall: keep an interface embeddings can plug into later.\n\nPhase BL-no-duplicates; decision D-no-duplicates; research R-dedupe-matchers.\n\nInterface fixed by tests/test_dedupe_eval.py (B-dedupe-evalset): ddflow.services.similar.build(records) -> index, records being mappings with id, kind, title, body; index.query(record, limit=None) -> list[tuple[id, score]] best first, scores in [0, 1], record a mapping with kind, title, body; limit=None returns every candidate scored above zero; the query's own id may appear (the evaluation drops it). The test scores each labelled pair as an add sees it (the later record queries the earlier records of its group: bugs among bugs, tasks/phases among items), with pessimistic tie ranks, ASK_THRESHOLD 0.55, and also requires >= 25% of duplicates to score >= the ask threshold (so precision is not vacuous). Remove the strict xfail on test_the_engine_meets_the_bar when the engine lands; test_the_reference_matcher_meets_the_bar shows the research matcher clears the bar (dup R@3 0.951, related R@5 0.957, lenient P 0.824, hard negatives above 0.15)."},"id":"eda7aa647ea6cca0e585ec9c8","kind":"task.updated","lamport":7165,"schema":1,"subject":"B-similar-engine","ts":"2026-10-01T21:27:06.119262Z"}
